      "triangles" : 752660,
      "radius" : 0.20168040791125297,
      "document" : "# Shooter - Overview [[reset]]\nA turret-mounted flywheel shooter for 6 in diameter balls, designed to fire at up to 18 balls per second. Two motors drive the flywheels and a third motor drives the adjustable hood, which pivots on the same axis as the flywheel. Start with the [[reset|assembled view]], or [[animate:0,1,2500|watch it come apart]].\n\n[[preset:Preset 1|Animate me]]\n\n# Requirements [[explode:0]]\n- Ball: 6 in diameter.\n- Fire rate: 18 balls per second, so the flywheels must recover speed between shots almost instantly.\n- Adjustable shot angle without moving the flywheel.\n- Compact enough to rotate on a turret ring.\n\n# Flywheels [[explode:0.5]]\nTwo motors power the flywheels. Splitting the load across two motors gives the torque to hold wheel speed at the full 18 balls per second instead of sagging after the first few shots. [[highlight:1,2|Highlight the first two parts]] or [[all|clear the highlight]].\n\n# Hood [[explode:0.8]]\nOne motor drives the hood. The hood rotates about the flywheel axis, so the gap between the hood and the wheel stays constant (ball compression never changes) while the exit angle sweeps. [[isolate:1,2,3|Isolate a few parts]] then [[all|show everything]] again.\n\n# Turret ring [[preset:Preset 1]]\nThe whole shooter rides on a geared ring so it can aim independently of the drivetrain. This heading plays the saved preset \"Preset 1\"; you can also [[preset:Preset 2|play Preset 2]].\n\n# Results [[reset]]\nReplace this section with test data: measured fire rate, wheel speed recovery time, and shot consistency at each hood angle.\n",
